                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Needs a save-state option because most of the later levels are designed to be a long tedious slog where one mistake means you have to start over.  Some levels it takes 5 minutes just to scope it out first to figure out what you need to do, since there's no panning, and then could be up to 15 minutes of pushing blocks around plus retries.  That one thing would solve every problem with the game -- it's clever and engaging otherwise.  Matches the original (except for one little timing thing that doesn't matter).",
